1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,649
Welcome to the second episode of Earthlings
101. Today you will learn about the origin

2
00:00:04,649 --> 00:00:09,600
of life on earth. Most earthlings think their
life originated in the oceans of young earth.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:16,600
But actually, it came from space - on a stray
missile from the Squid War.

4
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:52,780
The missile that plunged into the oceans of young
earth didn't contain any explosive, nuclear

5
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:59,370
or quantum collapse charge. It's payload consisted
of two million specimen of a simple, carbon-based,

6
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:03,829
self-replicating nano weapon, a primitive
variant of the dreaded grey goo. By the way,

7
00:01:03,829 --> 00:01:07,930
earthlings would call this a bio-weapon, or
artificial life form, but only because life

8
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:10,170
on earth has developed from this weapon.

9
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,470
You may remember the Squid War from early
history class. It was a merciless war between

10
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:18,190
the then Andromeda Dominion and the old Squid
Kingdom, fought with all means authorized

11
00:01:18,190 --> 00:01:23,290
by the central bureaucracy. The Dominion eventually
crushed the Squids, but their victory application

12
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:26,659
was rejected by the bureaucracy because they
couldn't account for one of the three million

13
00:01:26,659 --> 00:01:31,320
planetary missiles fired in this war: The
very missile that had found its way to earth.

14
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:36,979
The bio-weapon was based on carbon. Most nanolabs
use carbon to build artificial life forms,

15
00:01:36,979 --> 00:01:41,750
simply because carbon atoms are ideal building
blocks. See, the bonds an atom can make is

16
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:46,270
defined by the electrons and free slots in
their outer electron shell. A covalent bond

17
00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:50,440
is an electron-sharing-deal between two atoms
: I put an electron in your slot, you put

18
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:56,220
an electron into mine. So, Fluorine can make
one bond, oxygen can make two, nitrogen can

19
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:01,820
make three, carbon can make four. Boron has
five slots but only three electrons to share,

20
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:06,520
so it can make three bonds, Beryllium can
make two, and Lithium one. That's why carbon

21
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:10,539
is the nano’technicians best friend: With
no less than 4 connections per atom you can

22
00:02:10,539 --> 00:02:15,980
build a lot of things: chains, grids, rings,
- you name it. With some other atoms Like

23
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:20,940
oxygen or nitrogen here and there, and the
free slots plugged with tiny hydrogen atoms,

24
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:25,209
building nano machines is as easy as playing
with construction kits for young aliens.

25
00:02:25,209 --> 00:02:29,450
So, back to our nano weapon which has just
been released in the warm oceans of young

26
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:34,390
earth. Those weapons work like viral religions:
A viral religion consist basically of a set

27
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:37,849
of instructions to make the believers spread
the religion, which may or may not involve

28
00:02:37,849 --> 00:02:42,660
killing non-believers. Self-replicating nano
weapons work the same way - only without the

29
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:47,420
believers. The instructions come usually with
some moleculary nanomachines called enzymes

30
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:51,959
which perform the actual replication, and
a wrapping to hold it all together.

31
00:02:51,959 --> 00:02:56,190
In this case, the instructions were written
on a molecule called DNA, it's basically a

32
00:02:56,190 --> 00:03:01,770
primitive variant of XNA, the trademark molecule
of the Arctarian nanolabs, which is not surprising

33
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:05,959
as the Arctarian weapon factories supplied
both sides during the Squid War.

34
00:03:05,959 --> 00:03:10,620
The DNA of these ancient bio-weapons contained
usually instructions for self-replication,

35
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:15,379
plus an actual message which was often an
insult, like, "Eat this, tentacle heads!"

36
00:03:15,379 --> 00:03:20,010
or "Fisheaters must die!", or in this case,
"Squids are stupid"

37
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:26,610
So, those little bags of DNA and enzymes started
self-replicating. Unfortunately, replicating

38
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:30,879
isn't of much use if you don't have a source
for new bio-mass. The creature was designed

39
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:35,629
to replicate on a squid planet which was rich
on elementary carbon, so biomass wasn't supposed

40
00:03:35,629 --> 00:03:40,780
to be an issue. But here, on earth, elementary
carbon was rare. That's where the creature

41
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:44,129
started to evolve - the beginning of life
on earth.

42
00:03:44,129 --> 00:03:48,400
Let me get this straight: life on earth is
wholly different from life anywhere else.

43
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:52,340
In the whole Galaxy, the evolution of life
is regulated by the all-mighty and omnipresent

44
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:57,409
Galactic Bureaucracy. When a planet is approved
for developing life, it is put under the responsibility

45
00:03:57,409 --> 00:04:01,870
of an approved bio-administrator who comes
from an advanced civilization of class 14

46
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:07,720
or higher. The administrator supervises evolution,
decides on creation of new species, approves

47
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:12,860
mutations, oversees the development of civilisation
and, most important of all, does all the administrative

48
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:18,380
steps required by the galactic bureau of planetary
evolution, which means quite a lot of paperwork.

49
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:21,660
The official goal of all this is to create
sentient life and make it reach the point

50
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:26,500
where it develops the concept of money so
that it can pay taxes. But the real goal of

51
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:30,610
every bio-administrator is to push the lifeforms
on the planet to develop scripture, from which

52
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:35,530
point on they can do their own paperwork and
the administrator can leave the planet.

53
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:40,870
However, as mentioned in the last episode,
earth is out of reach of the galactic bureaucracy.

54
00:04:40,870 --> 00:04:45,900
In consequence, life on earth follows a completely
unregulated, wild evolution, an explosion

55
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:51,400
of life limited only by natural resources.
In one word, any bio-anarchists wet dream,

56
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:56,190
and any bio-administrator's nightmare.
This is, by the way, the reason why the Dominion

57
00:04:56,190 --> 00:05:00,110
never officially admitted that they lost their
missile on earth.

58
00:05:00,110 --> 00:05:05,550
Uncontrolled evolution is based on three mechanisms:
replication, mutation and natural selection.

59
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:09,880
The simplest form of replication is duplicating
the code and the individual. There is another

60
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:14,720
form of replication called sexual reproduction,
which we will discuss later.

61
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:18,790
Mutation is often misunderstood. It doesn't
consist in having a tentacle growing out of

62
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:23,520
one's head after receiving a bit too much
radiation. That may be the case for Tangerian

63
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:28,240
Metamutants, but it's not how it works on
earth. On earth, mutation means a usually

64
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:33,699
small variation in the offspring due to damaged
genetic code - say, a different skin color,

65
00:05:33,699 --> 00:05:35,400
or stronger leg muscles.

66
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:40,110
As for natural selection, it means that nature
favours individuals which are good at feeding,

67
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:45,349
reproducing and not dying. Humans usually
paraphrase this as "survival of the fittest"

68
00:05:45,349 --> 00:05:49,449
. This might be correct, as long as survival
and fitness serve the ultimate purpose: Spreading

69
00:05:49,449 --> 00:05:53,540
the code. The code doesn't care about the
about the well-being of the individual, as

70
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:58,259
long as it is spread. If this means being
eaten by your offspring, evolution is fine

71
00:05:58,259 --> 00:05:58,820
with it.

72
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:02,729
A simple example of natural selection would
be an animal running from a predator. If by

73
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:07,240
chance it has grown a fifth leg allowing to
outrun the predator - great. But actually,

74
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:11,940
it is enough - and far more probable - to
run just a little bit faster than one's sibling.

75
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:16,410
This way, even small variations may make the
difference between dying and surviving. With

76
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:21,340
time, these variations will accumulate and
the species will become faster and faster.

77
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:26,139
But back to our little organism. It needed
carbon to multiply, but carbon was only available

78
00:06:26,139 --> 00:06:32,300
in form of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere.
Besides this, there were pretty useless nitrogen,

79
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:37,250
and tons of hydric acid - you know, this disgusting
liquid which covers two thirds of the planet.

80
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:42,320
So, evolution kicked in and our organisms
developed a method to transform carbon dioxide

81
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:47,889
into bio-mass. In its evolved form, this process
is called photosynthesis.

82
00:06:47,889 --> 00:06:51,840
Photosynthesis consists basically in using
sunlight to transform carbon dioxide and hydric

83
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:56,449
acid into oxygen and a chemical called sugar.
Oxygen is a toxic substance which had to be

84
00:06:56,449 --> 00:07:00,880
released into the atmosphere, but sugar is
pretty useful : It comes in different variants

85
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:05,800
and can be used for short-term energy storage
and to obtain bio-mass. You can also use it

86
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:10,669
to build chains to obtain starch for long-term
energy storage, or cellulose for structural

87
00:07:10,669 --> 00:07:12,419
reinforcement.

88
00:07:12,419 --> 00:07:16,270
Photosynthesis is still used by plants on
earth to build their bio-mass. It's noteworthy

89
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:20,960
that only one fifteenth of the sugar created
by photosynthesis comes from the hydric acid

90
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:26,090
- actually, only the tiny hydrogen atoms used
to plug the free slots. The rest comes form

91
00:07:26,090 --> 00:07:31,850
carbon dioxide. So, when you visit earth and
find gigantic forests made of plants, remember

92
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:34,860
that 93% of their dry matter is made off "air".

93
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:39,509
Now that our little organism knew how to literally
create bio-mass out of thin air, it multiplied

94
00:07:39,509 --> 00:07:44,729
and took over the whole planet. While doing
so, it evolved into a variety of species,

95
00:07:44,729 --> 00:07:49,460
some of which developed a number of improvements,
for example a cell core, tiny tentacles to

96
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:54,770
move around, or sexual reproduction - basically
mixing the codes of two individuals to create

97
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:59,280
a new one. We will learn more about sexual
reproduction in the next episode.

98
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:04,009
Everything seemed fine for our little light-eating
organisms. But after a while, a problem came

99
00:08:04,009 --> 00:08:09,539
up. Remember oxygen, this toxic by product
of photosynthesis ? This stuff had accumulated

100
00:08:09,539 --> 00:08:13,870
in the atmosphere and now reached a dangerous
concentration. This could have been the end

101
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:18,430
of life on earth - but luckily, one organism
mutated and found a way of transforming oxygen

102
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:23,840
and sugar back into carbon dioxide, hydric
acid and energy. This is called respiration,

103
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:26,210
and it's basically photosynthesis backwards.

104
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:31,130
Now we had two kinds of creatures: Light eaters
- also known as plants - who create sugar

105
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:36,989
and oxygen, and oxygen breathers, also called
animals, who transform sugar and oxygen back

106
00:08:36,989 --> 00:08:42,769
into carbon dioxide. But how did the animals
get the sugar ? Well, by devouring plants!

107
00:08:42,769 --> 00:08:46,929
Soon those animals multiplied and lowered
the oxygen level in the atmosphere. Since

108
00:08:46,929 --> 00:08:50,779
then, plants and animals share the planet,
and each group produces the gas the other

109
00:08:50,779 --> 00:08:51,540
group needs.

110
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:56,389
But evolution didn't stop there. With time,
it grew creatures which were better and better

111
00:08:56,389 --> 00:09:02,449
at feeding, reproducing and not dying. The
light-eating cells became multicellular plants,

112
00:09:02,449 --> 00:09:06,850
conquered the oceans and then the land . The
oxygen-breathers evolved into multicellular

113
00:09:06,850 --> 00:09:11,569
animals, and developed traits like symmetry,
a neural system and an inclination for moving

114
00:09:11,569 --> 00:09:17,129
around. One branch evolved into small creatures
with an exoskeleton called insects. Others

115
00:09:17,129 --> 00:09:21,259
developed an endoskeleton, eyes and a mouth
and eventually crawled onto land and grew

116
00:09:21,259 --> 00:09:22,389
legs.

117
00:09:22,389 --> 00:09:29,279
Most species of this time are extinct by now
- except for, the microbes.

118
00:09:29,279 --> 00:09:33,649
Strategic advice! If you want to extinguish
all humans and animals on earth to prepare

119
00:09:33,649 --> 00:09:39,139
it for colonization, don't forget the insects!
They are everywhere, they are hard to kill,

120
00:09:39,139 --> 00:09:41,509
and they can be really, really annoying.

121
00:09:41,509 --> 00:09:45,629
The most obvious difference between plants
and animals is that animals move around, whereas

122
00:09:45,629 --> 00:09:51,779
plants stay at one place. Why is this so?
Well, animals have to seek edible plants,

123
00:09:51,779 --> 00:09:56,819
or run after other animals, whereas plants
feed on air, hydric acid and sunlight, resources

124
00:09:56,819 --> 00:10:02,549
which are available everywhere. However, spreading
one's DNA isn't easy when you can't move.

125
00:10:02,549 --> 00:10:06,879
So, plants eventually found a way to get animals
to carry their DNA around.

126
00:10:06,879 --> 00:10:12,459
Remember sugar, the main product of photosynthesis?
Animals love that stuff, as it's easy to process

127
00:10:12,459 --> 00:10:16,720
and rich on energy. Normally, plants don't
store large amounts of sugar because they

128
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:21,720
don't want to get eaten. But now, they developed
exposed sugar-filled sexual organs called

129
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:26,779
flowers to bribe insects into carrying their
DNA to other plants for sexual reproduction.

130
00:10:26,779 --> 00:10:31,089
Then they put their seed into delicious sugar
packages called fruits to bribe bigger animals

131
00:10:31,089 --> 00:10:33,059
into carrying their seed around.

132
00:10:33,059 --> 00:10:37,220
Both fruits an flowers are colored to attract
the attention of animals. In the language

133
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:42,889
of plants, bright colors mean "Here is sugar".
Animals, on the other side, don't want parts

134
00:10:42,889 --> 00:10:47,470
of their body to be eaten, so in the language
of animals, bright colors either mean "I'm

135
00:10:47,470 --> 00:10:52,049
poisonous", or, "Catch me if you can, I have
wings!".

136
00:10:52,049 --> 00:10:58,029
All those plants, insects, fruit-eaters, predators
and microbes form a complex, self regulating

137
00:10:58,029 --> 00:11:02,199
system, without any need of a bio-administrator.
Earthlings call this an ecosystem.

138
00:11:02,199 --> 00:11:07,730
Scientific advice. A popular experiment among
students consists in abducting an earthling,

139
00:11:07,730 --> 00:11:11,829
a cellulose-eating animal and some plants
and putting them into a tank in order to create

140
00:11:11,829 --> 00:11:16,739
a micro-ecosystem. But this doesn't work.
You get much better results when you put some

141
00:11:16,739 --> 00:11:20,819
ocean plants and animals into a small tank
filled with hydric acid.

142
00:11:20,819 --> 00:11:24,769
At some point, evolution led to bigger and
bigger animals, until the planet was ruled

143
00:11:24,769 --> 00:11:29,399
by giant creatures called dinosaurs. Some
of them evolved into small flying creatures

144
00:11:29,399 --> 00:11:33,769
called birds. Other creatures developed the
ability of nourishing their offspring with

145
00:11:33,769 --> 00:11:38,629
a liquid called milk. One branch of these
animals acquired some intelligence and dexterity

146
00:11:38,629 --> 00:11:43,869
in manipulating objects, and eventually evolved
into earthlings. The first earthlings lived

147
00:11:43,869 --> 00:11:48,449
pretty much like animals, collecting fruits,
hunting animals and protecting from predators

148
00:11:48,449 --> 00:11:52,949
- except that they developed their own tools
to do so. This is where natural evolution

149
00:11:52,949 --> 00:11:55,290
ends and civilization begins.

150
00:11:55,290 --> 00:12:00,079
Tips for tourists. If you are a time-traveller
and you visit the time of the dinosaurs, please

151
00:12:00,079 --> 00:12:04,509
don't take any dinosaurs with you. If it wasn't
for countless time tourists taking animals

152
00:12:04,509 --> 00:12:09,049
away as souvenirs or pets, dinosaurs wouldn't
be extinct.

153
00:12:09,049 --> 00:12:14,279
There is a small group of earthlings who might
not have developed by evolution. They call

154
00:12:14,279 --> 00:12:19,850
themselves creationists. According to their
own claims, they have been created by an extraterrestrial

155
00:12:19,850 --> 00:12:24,730
bio-engineer some thousands of solar cycles
ago. His intervention triggered an environmental

156
00:12:24,730 --> 00:12:29,290
catastrophe, an inundation with hydric acid
which killed all other life in the area. The

157
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:33,959
creationists, warned by their creator, saved
themselves onto a ship, crossed an ocean and

158
00:12:33,959 --> 00:12:37,660
settled in a place called America, where they
are waiting for their creator to pick them

159
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:43,109
up. However, the whole story seems unlikely
and doesn't fit the bureaucratic records.

160
00:12:43,109 --> 00:12:47,949
So most alien scientists agree that this story
has probably been made up by earthlings.

161
00:12:47,949 --> 00:12:52,259
In this episode, we have seen the evolution
that led to earthlings. This evolution was

162
00:12:52,259 --> 00:12:58,069
driven by one single force : An ancient code,
programmed to replicate itself at infinitum,

163
00:12:58,069 --> 00:13:01,829
unleashed in an uncontrolled environment,
pursuing its goal to the point of conquering

164
00:13:01,829 --> 00:13:06,170
a whole planet, of creating intelligent life
and of building a spacefaring civilization

165
00:13:06,170 --> 00:13:11,079
- and all this in order to deliver one simple
message : Squids are stupid.

166
00:13:11,079 --> 00:13:15,569
In the next episode we will learn more about
sexuality : How it works, how it alters the

167
00:13:15,569 --> 00:13:22,569
rules of evolution, and why it wouldn't even
exist if it wasn't for : parasites.

168
00:13:22,569 --> 00:13:29,569
Thank you for watching.

